WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.940
in April of 1861 when Abraham Lincoln issued&nbsp;
the first call for volunteers for the Union Army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.740
my great great grandfather Samuel Fletcher&nbsp;
Cheney joined the 21st Ohio volunteer Infantry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:24.240
he fought through all four years of the Civil&nbsp;
War from Chickamauga to Stones River to Atlanta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:32.400
he marched with his unit in The Grand Review&nbsp;
of troops a Pennsylvania Avenue in May of 1865.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.260
passed a reviewing stand where President&nbsp;
Johnson and General Grant were seated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:44.340
Silas Canfield the regimental historian&nbsp;
of the 21st Ohio volunteer Infantry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:52.560
describe the men in the unit this way he said&nbsp;
they had a just appreciation of the value and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:59.460
advantage of free government and the necessity&nbsp;
of Defending and maintaining it and they enlisted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:08.160
prepared to accept all the necessary labors&nbsp;
fatigues exposures dangers and even death for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:15.600
the unity of our nation and the perpetuity of our&nbsp;
institutions I have found myself thinking often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:22.320
especially since January 6th of my great great&nbsp;
grandfather and all those in every generation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.260
who have sacrificed so much for the unity of our&nbsp;
nation and the perpetuity of our institutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.140
at the heart of our Republic is the&nbsp;
guarantee of the peaceful transfer of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:41.220
members of Congress are reminded of this every&nbsp;
day as we pass through the capital Rotunda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:46.260
their eight magnificent paintings&nbsp;
detailed the earliest days of our Republic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:56.040
one painted by John Trumbull depicts the moment&nbsp;
in 1793. when George Washington resigned his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:03.120
commission handing control of the Continental&nbsp;
Army back to Congress Trumbull called this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:10.560
quote one of the highest moral lessons ever&nbsp;
given the world with this Noble act George&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.500
Washington established the indispensable example&nbsp;
of the peaceful transfer of power in our nation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:24.240
standing on the west front of the Capitol in 1981&nbsp;
President Ronald Reagan described it this way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:32.280
the orderly transfer of authority is called for in&nbsp;
the Constitution routinely takes place as it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:39.780
for almost two centuries and few of us stopped to&nbsp;
think how unique we really are in the eyes of many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:46.680
in the world this every four-year ceremony that&nbsp;
we accept as normal is nothing less than a miracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:53.760
every president in our history has defended&nbsp;
this orderly transfer of authority except one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:02.580
January 6 2021 was the first time one American&nbsp;
president refused his constitutional duty to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:09.480
transfer power peacefully to the next in our work&nbsp;
over the last 18 months the select committee has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:14.280
recognized Our obligation to do everything&nbsp;
we can to ensure this never happens again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.860
at the beginning of our investigation&nbsp;
we understood that tens of millions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:25.740
Americans had been persuaded by President&nbsp;
Trump that the 2020 election was stolen by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:31.800
overwhelming fraud and we also knew this was&nbsp;
flatly false we knew that dozens of state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:37.140
and federal judges had addressed and resolved&nbsp;
all manner of allegations about the election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:43.380
our legal system functioned as it should but&nbsp;
our president would not accept the outcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:51.300
among the most shameful of this committee's&nbsp;
findings was that President Trump sat in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:57.420
the dining room off the Oval Office watching&nbsp;
the violent riot at the Capitol on television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:04.500
for hours he would not issue a public statement&nbsp;
instructing his supporters to disperse and leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:11.280
the capitol despite urgent pleas from his White&nbsp;
House staff and dozens of others to do so members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:17.640
of his family his White House lawyers virtually&nbsp;
all those around him knew that this simple Act&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:26.580
was critical for hours he would not do it during&nbsp;
this time law enforcement agents were attacked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:32.940
and seriously injured the capital was invaded the&nbsp;
Electoral count was halted and the lives of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:39.840
in the capital were put at risk in addition to&nbsp;
being unlawful as described in our report this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:47.220
was an utter moral failure and a clear dereliction&nbsp;
of Duty evidence of this can be seen in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:52.380
testimony of President Trump's own White House&nbsp;
Council and several other White House Witnesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.640 --> 00:05:01.740
no man who would behave that way at that moment in&nbsp;
time can ever serve in any position of authority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:11.400
in our nation again he is unfit for any office the&nbsp;
committee recognizes that our work has only begun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.560
it's only the initial step in addressing president&nbsp;
Trump's effort to remain in office illegally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:22.200
prosecutors are considering the implications&nbsp;
of the conduct that we describe in our report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:33.360
as our citizens all across our nation in 1761 John&nbsp;
Adams wrote the very ground of our liberties is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:39.120
the freedom of Elections faith in our elections&nbsp;
and the rule of law is Paramount to our Republic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:47.520
election deniers those who refuse to accept lawful&nbsp;
election results purposely attack the rule of law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:55.020
and the foundation of our country the history of&nbsp;
our time will show that The Bravery of a handful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.020 --> 00:06:02.160
of Americans doing their Duty saved us from an&nbsp;
even more grave constitutional crisis elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:08.160
officials election workers and public servants&nbsp;
stood against Donald Trump's corrupt pressure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:14.940
many of our committee's Witnesses showed selfless&nbsp;
patriotism and their words and courage will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:21.960
be remembered the brave men and women of the&nbsp;
Capitol Police the Metropolitan Police and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:28.500
the other law enforcement officers who fought to&nbsp;
defend us that day saved lives and our democracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.420
finally I wish to thank my&nbsp;
colleagues on this committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.780
it has been a tremendous honor to serve with&nbsp;
all of you we have accomplished great and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:46.440
important things together and I hope we have set&nbsp;
an example and I also want to thank all of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:53.280
who have honorably contributed to the work of our&nbsp;
committee and to our report we have accomplished&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:59.220
much over a short period of time many of you&nbsp;
sacrificed for the good of our nation you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:06.180
helped make history and I hope helped to write&nbsp;
the ship thank you Mr chairman I yield back

